      "writtenOn": "2025-10-31T16:09:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why check if apic_regs is not NULL but don\u0027t check if apic is not NULL?",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7172676_e93e8bb4",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 368,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-02T03:53:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As `vcpu-\u003earch.apic` is checked in `pkvm_pin_shared_vcpu`. If `vcpu-\u003earch.apic` is NULL, then we will not be here.\n\nBut considering the discussion in aosp/3783090, if the host doesn\u0027t have `lapic_in_kernel`(which means the host user space VMM doesn\u0027t create irqchip via vm_ioctl KVM_CREATE_IRQCHIP and `irqchip_mode \u003d\u003d KVM_IRQCHIP_NONE`), `vcpu-\u003earch.apic` will be NULL, then checking apic is also needed here.",
      "parentUuid": "4786a6d8_9d8a5bd7",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bfbdd6c6_8445afc6",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 368,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-02T14:13:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In any case, if apic is not NULL, apic_regs should be also not NULL (and we should return an error in pkvm_pin_shared_vcpu() if apic is non-NULL but apic_regs is NULL), so checking specifically apic_regs here is not necessary?",
      "parentUuid": "f7172676_e93e8bb4",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07aabae5_6103a5e9",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 368,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-03T00:46:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, in this unpin function, only needs to check `vcpu-\u003earch.apic`.",
      "parentUuid": "bfbdd6c6_8445afc6",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99ace6f3_d3277a84",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 368,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-03T04:07:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is better to check apic_regs as well, since we got apic_regs from the apic memory which is owned by the host, not owned by the pKVM. A malicious host may change the apic_regs as a NULL pointer.",
      "parentUuid": "07aabae5_6103a5e9",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "819e817d_c37e714b",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 381,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-31T16:09:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we actually require vcpu-\u003earch.apic to be non-NULL? i.e. do we actually enforce in-kernel irqchip?",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a5232bf_c7234395",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 381,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-02T03:53:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, if the host user space VMM doesn\u0027t create irqchip, then host will not allocate apic memory page.",
      "parentUuid": "819e817d_c37e714b",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b91b8f04_3b889720",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 402,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-31T16:09:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While we\u0027re at it, this comment sounds like lapic_in_kernel() is the only thing use vcpu-\u003earch.apic for (which would mean that we don\u0027t really need to share this memory with hypervisor).\n\nWhereas it looks like pKVM actually uses vcpu-\u003earch.apic-\u003eregs at least for VIRTUAL_APIC_PAGE_ADDR (which is BTW quite critical, right?), plus in some other places, at least in kvm_lapic_readable_reg_mask().\n\nSo this comment is misleading?\n\n...And BTW speaking of kvm_lapic_readable_reg_mask(), it seems to check some things that may change at runtime (apic_x2apic_mode() and kvm_lapic_lvt_supported())? So isn\u0027t it a problem that kvm_lapic_readable_reg_mask() in pKVM  relies on the initial snapshot on the host\u0027s APIC state, captured at vCPU creation time, not the up-to-date APIC state?",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d537e978_5677fa40",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 402,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-02T03:53:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So this comment is misleading?\n\nSure, I can enhance this comment.\n\n\u003e ...And BTW speaking of kvm_lapic_readable_reg_mask(), it seems to check some things that may change at runtime (apic_x2apic_mode() and kvm_lapic_lvt_supported())? So isn\u0027t it a problem that kvm_lapic_readable_reg_mask() in pKVM relies on the initial snapshot on the host\u0027s APIC state, captured at vCPU creation time, not the up-to-date APIC state?\n\nThe pKVM\u0027s kvm_vcpu-\u003earch.apic points to host\u0027s kvm_vcpu-\u003earch.apic, so apic_x2apic_mode() and kernel_lapic_lvt_supported() should be update-to-date APIC state. What is not good, is that, apic_x2apic_mode() checks the apic_base via apic-\u003evcpu-\u003earch.apic_base, which means the pKVM hypervisor access the host\u0027s kvm_vcpu via the pointer stored in apic, not via the pointer in its pkvm_vcpu. The apic_base in pKVM\u0027s kvm_vcpu-\u003earch is also update-to-date via pkvm_set_virtual_apic_mode, probably can re-write kvm_lapic_readable_reg_mask() for pKVM if necessary, for v6.18?.",
      "parentUuid": "b91b8f04_3b889720",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7dd7a31e_f841bd62",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 402,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-02T14:13:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The pKVM\u0027s kvm_vcpu-\u003earch.apic points to host\u0027s kvm_vcpu-\u003earch.apic, so apic_x2apic_mode() and kernel_lapic_lvt_supported() should be update-to-date APIC state.\n\nAh, indeed. I\u0027ve been contradicting myself. :) \n\n\u003e What is not good, is that, apic_x2apic_mode() checks the apic_base via apic-\u003evcpu-\u003earch.apic_base, which means the pKVM hypervisor access the host\u0027s kvm_vcpu via the pointer stored in apic, not via the pointer in its pkvm_vcpu.\n\nDo you mean there is a potential security issue? i.e. with a correctly working host it should work correctly (and the host\u0027s kvm_vcpu is shared with pKVM anyway), but a malicious host may change its apic-\u003evcpu to point to any address?\n\n\u003e probably can re-write kvm_lapic_readable_reg_mask() for pKVM if necessary, for v6.18?.\n\nYeah, I guess in 6.15+ we want to implement it in a secure way anyway. And then it shouldn\u0027t be hard to backport that to 6.12 later.",
      "parentUuid": "d537e978_5677fa40",
      "revId": "5045bc5be134d871f0115ca28e731fa74201af75",
